# Line endings.
#
# Windows checkouts default to CRLF, which silently breaks two things here:
#   * db/init/01-databases.sh is bind-mounted into the Linux MariaDB container.
#     With CRLF the container fails with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" and the
#     database + users are never created — the gateway then cannot connect and
#     the failure looks like a password problem.
#   * migrations/*.sql and the Dockerfile are read inside Linux images too.
#
# Anything that ends up inside a container, or is run by bash, is pinned to LF
# regardless of the developer's platform. PowerShell/batch files are pinned to
# CRLF, which cmd.exe requires for .bat/.cmd.

* text=auto

*.sh      text eol=lf
*.sql     text eol=lf
*.conf    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.env     text eol=lf
*.example text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Makefile  text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
go.mod    text eol=lf
go.sum    text eol=lf
*.go      text eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary
*.tgz  binary
*.ico  binary
*.exe  binary
